WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.690
In Genesis, God says: every moving
thing that lives will be food for you.

2
00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:09.360
Yet many people today
refuse to eat meat at all.

3
00:00:09.410 --> 00:00:13.540
And in laboratories, some new
medicines are tested on animals.

4
00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:19.150
In 1975, the philosopher Peter Singer
argued that what matters morally is the

5
00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:22.240
ability to suffer, not species.

6
00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:27.020
So can it ever be right to eat
animals, or to test medicines on them?

7
00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:30.960
In this mission, you'll learn the
difference between animal welfare and animal

8
00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:34.220
rights, and why sentience matters.

9
00:00:34.270 --> 00:00:38.240
Then you'll read what the Bible and
Catholic teaching say about animals,

10
00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:40.490
and weigh up Singer's challenge.

11
00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:46.520
Your mission: weigh up when, if ever, it is
right to use animals for food or medicine.
